Mesa M2: flush_frontbuffer must tolerate a NULL context

The gallium X11 frontend presents without a bound context:
xmesa_swap_st_framebuffer() calls xmesa_st_framebuffer_display(drawable, NULL,
...), so screen->flush_frontbuffer arrives with ctx == NULL.  virgl's
implementation passed that straight to virgl_flush_eq(), which reads
ctx->cbuf at offset 0x4e0 -- a NULL dereference on every swap (measured in the
first M2 boot: rip at the top of virgl_flush_eq, rdi == 0).

It is also unnecessary: XMesaSwapBuffers() runs
st_context_flush(st, ST_FLUSH_FRONT, &fence, ...) *before* the display call, so
the batch is already submitted.  Guard the flush and pass the (absent) command
buffer through; every winsys that does not need it ignores it, and ours does.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_screen.c
@@ -774,8 +774,16 @@
    struct virgl_context *vctx = virgl_context(ctx);
 
    if (vws->flush_frontbuffer) {
-      virgl_flush_eq(vctx, vctx, NULL);
-      vws->flush_frontbuffer(vws, vctx->cbuf, vres->hw_res, level, layer, winsys_drawable_handle,
+      /* The X11 frontend presents with ctx == NULL: xmesa_swap_st_framebuffer()
+       * calls xmesa_st_framebuffer_display(drawable, NULL, ...), so `ctx` here
+       * is NULL and virgl_flush_eq() dereferences it (measured: a NULL-context
+       * SIGSEGV at the top of virgl_flush_eq on every swap, M2).  Nothing needs
+       * flushing in that case anyway -- XMesaSwapBuffers() already submitted the
+       * batch through st_context_flush(st, ST_FLUSH_FRONT, ...). */
+      if (ctx)
+         virgl_flush_eq(vctx, vctx, NULL);
+      vws->flush_frontbuffer(vws, ctx ? vctx->cbuf : NULL, vres->hw_res, level,
+                             layer, winsys_drawable_handle,
                              nboxes == 1 ? sub_box : NULL);
    }
 }
